from lib import *
C=10;S='maths'
CH='geometry'
lesson(C,S,CH,'similar-triangles-and-thales',"Similar triangles and Thales (Basic Proportionality) theorem","The shadow of a tree","At noon a 2 m stick casts a 1 m shadow while a tree casts a 6 m shadow. Because the sun's rays make the same angle, the two triangles have the same shape. How tall is the tree?",
["Two triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are in the same ratio. @ similar triangles",
 "Thales (Basic Proportionality) theorem: a line drawn parallel to one side of a triangle divides the other two sides in the same ratio. @ Thales theorem",
 "In triangle ABC with DE parallel to BC, AD/DB = AE/EC. @ AD/DB = AE/EC",
 "The converse is also true: if a line divides two sides in the same ratio, it is parallel to the third side. @ converse",
 "The angle bisector of a triangle divides the opposite side in the ratio of the other two sides. @ angle bisector theorem",
 "Similarity tests: AA (two equal angles), SSS (three proportional sides) and SAS (one equal angle and the including sides proportional). @ AA, SSS, SAS",
 "For similar triangles, the ratio of areas equals the square of the ratio of corresponding sides. @ area ratio = side ratio squared"],
("In triangle ABC, DE is parallel to BC with D on AB and E on AC. If AD = 3, DB = 6 and AE = 2, find EC.",[("By Thales: AD/DB = AE/EC, so 3/6 = 2/EC.","The parallel line divides the sides proportionally."),("Cross-multiply: 3 x EC = 12.","From 3/6 = 2/EC."),("EC = 4.","Check: 2/4 = 1/2 = 3/6.")]),
("State Thales theorem and one test for similar triangles.",["Parallel line divides sides in the same ratio","AA test","Areas are in ratio of squares of sides"],["Using the ratio of areas as the ratio of sides"]),
["DE parallel to BC gives AD/DB = AE/EC.","AA, SSS and SAS prove similarity.","Area ratio = (side ratio) squared.","Angle bisector divides the opposite side in the ratio of the other two sides."],
["m|In triangle ABC with DE parallel to BC, AD/DB =|AE/EC|AB/AC~That compares whole sides;BC/DE~Not the Thales ratio|Thales theorem.",
 "n|If two similar triangles have sides in ratio 1 : 3, the ratio of their areas is 1 : x. Find x.|9|3 squared = 9.",
 "t|Two triangles with two equal angles are similar.|True|AA test.",
 "n|DE parallel to BC. AD = 4, DB = 8, AE = 3. Find EC.|6|4/8 = 3/EC gives EC = 6.",
 "t|All squares are similar.|True|Same angles and sides in equal ratio.",
 "t|All rectangles are similar.|False|Sides need not be in the same ratio.",
 "n|A 2 m stick has a 1 m shadow. A tree has a 6 m shadow. The tree's height in metres is|12|2/1 = h/6.",
 "s|The test that needs only two equal angles is the ____ test.|AA|Angle-Angle."],
svg=(tri([(230,30),(80,250),(380,250)],['A','B','C'],'<line x1="155" y1="140" x2="305" y2="140" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="3"/><text x="125" y="140">D</text><text x="310" y="140">E</text><text x="190" y="285" font-size="14">DE parallel to BC: AD/DB = AE/EC</text>'),"Triangle ABC with a line DE parallel to the base BC","Thales theorem"))
lesson(C,S,CH,'pythagoras-theorem',"Pythagoras theorem and its converse","The ladder","A 5 m ladder leans on a wall with its foot 3 m from the wall. How high does it reach? A right-angled triangle hides inside this picture.",
["In a right-angled triangle the side opposite the right angle is the hypotenuse, the longest side. @ hypotenuse",
 "Pythagoras theorem: the square on the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares on the other two sides, c squared = a squared + b squared. @ c^2 = a^2 + b^2",
 "For the ladder, height squared = 5 squared - 3 squared = 25 - 9 = 16, so the height is 4 m. @ 3, 4, 5",
 "The converse: if c squared = a squared + b squared in a triangle, then the angle opposite c is a right angle. @ converse",
 "Common Pythagorean triples are 3, 4, 5; 5, 12, 13; 8, 15, 17 and 7, 24, 25. @ triples",
 "In a right triangle, the altitude to the hypotenuse makes two triangles similar to the whole, which gives another proof. @ altitude and similarity"],
("Is a triangle with sides 7, 24 and 25 right-angled?",[("The longest side is 25, so test 25 squared against 7 squared + 24 squared.","The hypotenuse must be the longest side."),("7 squared + 24 squared = 49 + 576 = 625 = 25 squared.","Calculate both sides."),("They are equal, so by the converse the triangle is right-angled.","The right angle is opposite the side of length 25.")]),
("State Pythagoras theorem and its converse.",["c squared = a squared + b squared","Hypotenuse is the longest side","Converse proves a right angle"],["Using the formula on a triangle that has no right angle"]),
["c squared = a squared + b squared in a right triangle.","Converse: if the equation holds, the triangle is right-angled.","3-4-5, 5-12-13, 8-15-17, 7-24-25 are triples.","Hypotenuse is opposite the right angle."],
["n|The hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs 6 and 8 is|10|36 + 64 = 100.",
 "t|Pythagoras theorem applies to every triangle.|False|Only to right-angled triangles.",
 "n|A ladder 13 m long reaches 12 m high. How far (m) is its foot from the wall?|5|169 - 144 = 25.",
 "m|Which is a right triangle?|5, 12, 13|4, 5, 6~16 + 25 is not 36;6, 7, 8~36 + 49 is not 64|25 + 144 = 169.",
 "n|The diagonal of a 12 by 5 rectangle is|13|144 + 25 = 169.",
 "t|The hypotenuse is the shortest side.|False|It is the longest.",
 "n|Legs 9 and 12; hypotenuse is|15|81 + 144 = 225.",
 "s|The side opposite the right angle is called the ____.|hypotenuse|By definition."],
svg=(tri([(80,250),(380,250),(80,60)],['B','C','A'],'<rect x="80" y="230" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="#333"/><text x="215" y="272" font-size="14">a</text><text x="45" y="160" font-size="14">b</text><text x="240" y="140" font-size="14">c</text><text x="120" y="25" font-size="14">c squared = a squared + b squared</text>'),"Right triangle with sides a, b and hypotenuse c","Pythagoras theorem"))
lesson(C,S,CH,'circles-and-tangents',"Circles and tangents","The wheel on the road","A wheel touches the straight road at just one point. A line that touches a circle at exactly one point is a tangent - the road is a tangent to the wheel.",
["A tangent to a circle touches it at exactly one point, called the point of contact. A secant cuts it in two points. @ tangent and secant",
 "The tangent at a point is perpendicular to the radius drawn to that point. @ tangent perpendicular to radius",
 "Two tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal in length. @ equal tangents",
 "So in the figure, if PA and PB are tangents from P, then PA = PB and the radii OA and OB make right angles with them. @ PA = PB",
 "The centre O lies on the bisector of the angle between the two tangents. @ angle bisector through O",
 "The length of the tangent from a point at distance d from the centre of a circle of radius r is the square root of (d squared - r squared). @ tangent length"],
("A point P is 13 cm from the centre O of a circle of radius 5 cm. Find the length of the tangent from P.",[("The radius to the point of contact is perpendicular to the tangent, so OAP is a right triangle with OP = 13 and OA = 5.","Tangent is perpendicular to the radius."),("PA squared = OP squared - OA squared = 169 - 25 = 144.","Pythagoras theorem."),("PA = 12 cm.","Square root of 144.")]),
("State two properties of tangents to a circle.",["Perpendicular to radius at the point of contact","Tangents from an external point are equal","Touches at exactly one point"],["Thinking a tangent meets the circle twice"]),
["A tangent meets the circle at exactly one point.","Tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact.","Tangents from an external point are equal in length.","Tangent length = square root of (d squared - r squared)."],
["m|A tangent touches a circle at|one point|two points~That is a secant;no point~It would be outside|By definition.",
 "n|The angle between the radius and the tangent at the point of contact is (degrees)|90|They are perpendicular.",
 "t|Tangents from an external point are equal in length.|True|Standard theorem.",
 "n|P is 10 cm from the centre of a circle of radius 6 cm. The tangent length (cm) is|8|100 - 36 = 64.",
 "t|A secant meets a circle at exactly one point.|False|That is a tangent; a secant meets it in two points.",
 "n|Tangent length 12 and radius 5: distance from the centre is|13|144 + 25 = 169.",
 "t|The centre lies on the angle bisector of the two tangents from an external point.|True|By symmetry.",
 "s|A line touching a circle at one point is a ____.|tangent|By definition."],
svg=(svg(460,300,'<circle cx="170" cy="150" r="85" fill="#d6eaf8" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="170" cy="150" r="3" fill="#333"/><text x="150" y="145">O</text><line x1="400" y1="150" x2="170" y2="150" stroke="#888" stroke-dasharray="4"/><line x1="255" y1="20" x2="255" y2="280" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="3"/><text x="260" y="145" font-size="14">A</text><text x="405" y="155">P</text><line x1="255" y1="150" x2="170" y2="150" stroke="#2471a3" stroke-width="2"/><text x="270" y="30" font-size="14">tangent</text><text x="200" y="170" font-size="13">r</text>'),"Circle with a tangent touching at A, radius OA perpendicular to the tangent","Tangent and radius"))
CH='coordinate-geometry'
lesson(C,S,CH,'distance-section-and-midpoint',"Distance, section formula and mid-point","The treasure map","A map has the school at (1, 2) and the temple at (7, 10). How far apart are they, and where is the point halfway? Coordinates answer both.",
["The distance between P(x1, y1) and Q(x2, y2) is the square root of [(x2 - x1) squared + (y2 - y1) squared]. @ distance formula",
 "It comes from Pythagoras theorem on a right triangle drawn between the points. @ Pythagoras",
 "The mid-point of PQ is ((x1 + x2)/2, (y1 + y2)/2). @ mid-point",
 "The point dividing PQ internally in the ratio m : n is ((m x2 + n x1)/(m + n), (m y2 + n y1)/(m + n)). @ section formula",
 "The points of trisection divide the segment in ratios 1 : 2 and 2 : 1. @ trisection",
 "The centroid of a triangle with vertices (x1,y1), (x2,y2), (x3,y3) is ((x1+x2+x3)/3, (y1+y2+y3)/3). @ centroid"],
("Find the distance between (1, 2) and (7, 10) and their mid-point.",[("Differences: 7 - 1 = 6 and 10 - 2 = 8.","Subtract coordinates."),("Distance = square root of (36 + 64) = 10.","This is a 6-8-10 right triangle."),("Mid-point = ((1+7)/2, (2+10)/2) = (4, 6).","Average each coordinate.")]),
("Write the distance, mid-point and section formulas in words.",["Distance from Pythagoras","Mid-point is the average","Section formula uses ratio m : n"],["Swapping m and n in the section formula"]),
["Distance = root of the sum of squared differences.","Mid-point = average of coordinates.","Section formula divides a segment in ratio m : n.","Centroid = average of the three vertices."],
["n|Distance between (0, 0) and (3, 4) is|5|9 + 16 = 25.",
 "m|Mid-point of (2, 4) and (6, 8) is|(4, 6)|(8, 12)~You added but did not halve;(2, 2)~You subtracted|Average each coordinate.",
 "t|Distance between two points is always positive or zero.|True|It is a square root of a sum of squares.",
 "n|Distance between (1, 1) and (4, 5) is|5|9 + 16 = 25.",
 "m|Centroid of (0,0), (6,0), (0,9) is|(2, 3)|(3, 4.5)~That is the mid-point of a side;(6, 9)~Sum, not average|Divide by 3.",
 "n|x-coordinate of the mid-point of (-2, 3) and (8, 7) is|3|(-2 + 8)/2.",
 "t|The section formula with m = n gives the mid-point.|True|m : n = 1 : 1.",
 "s|The point dividing a line segment into two equal parts is the ____.|mid-point|By definition."],
svg=(grid([(1,1,'P(1,1)'),(3,2,'M(3,2)'),(5,3,'Q(5,3)')],-1,5,[(1,1,5,3)]),"Two points and their mid-point on a grid","Mid-point between two points"))
